Models
# ...but not the q4nx-build converters, which live in a directory called
# models/ and are the one file every new family has to add. core.ignorecase is
# on by default on Windows, so "Models" matches it; the existing builders are
# tracked and unaffected, and a NEW one is silently not added.
!utilities/q4nx-build/q4nx/models/
!utilities/q4nx-build/q4nx/models/**
tmp

# open_npue AIE design sets -- BUILT, not checked in.
#
# These are the output of npu_offload/gemm_rtp/, which is the source. A binary
# in a repository beside the source that produces it is a claim nobody checks;
# ignoring them makes the rebuild the only way to get them, so the source
# cannot silently stop being the source.
#
# Build them with the commands in npu_offload/gemm_rtp/README.md. They are
# shipped pre-built in the distributed package only.
src/xclbins/BERT-h*/

# Claude Code: personal guidance is not shared (AGENTS.md is the shared doc).
#
# The skills SYMLINKS are deliberately NOT ignored. They point at
# .agents/skills/, which is the single source every other client reads, so they
# contain nothing personal -- and R1 requires them checked in, or a Claude user
# gets a different skill set from everyone else. Excluding the DIRECTORY (rather
# than its contents) would make that un-negotiable, because git cannot re-include
# a path whose parent directory is excluded -- hence `.claude/*` plus a negation.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
CLAUDE.md

# open_kernels build outputs and generated fixtures. A build directory is what it
# holds, not what it is called: an ablation or a kept reference copy is still one,
# and `build*/` alone let 1552 files into a `git add -A` (2026-09-13). Ignore the
# artifacts too, so a directory named anything at all cannot carry them in.
open_kernels/designs/*/build*/
open_kernels/designs/**/final.xclbin
open_kernels/designs/**/final.prj/
open_kernels/designs/**/insts.bin
open_kernels/designs/**/insts.elf
open_kernels/designs/*/*.bin
open_kernels/designs/*/*.cfg
# FA harness: float64 reference (make_test.py) and its shape sidecar
open_kernels/designs/*/*.npy
open_kernels/designs/*/*_meta.json
open_kernels/designs/*/*.log
open_kernels/harness/out/
open_kernels/model/out*/

# Generated kernel translation units (dense/, layer_x/, lm_head_q4/ and the
# gemv_q4 activation-prep entries): written per-spec by designs/*/gen_kernels.py
# (or on demand by gemv_q4.ensure_prep_entry / lm_head_q4._ensure_gy) during the
# export. They are NOT source -- the source is the generator + the recipe -- so
# they are regenerated at build time and never tracked. A tracked copy drifts to
# match whichever spec was exported last.
open_kernels/designs/dense/*.cc
open_kernels/designs/layer_x/*.cc
open_kernels/designs/lm_head_q4/*.cc
open_kernels/designs/gemv_q4/gemv_q4_prep_k*.cc
open_kernels/designs/gemm_q4/*.cc
open_kernels/designs/gemm_q4/layout_m*.txt

# npu_offload/matmul generated fixtures (make_test.py) and run configs
npu_offload/matmul/[abyr]_m*.bin
npu_offload/matmul/ref_m*.bin
npu_offload/matmul/run_m*.cfg
src/open_qwen36/out/
src/open_whisper/out/

# Open Qwen3.6-MoE kernel sets -- BUILT, not checked in.
#
# The source is open_kernels/designs/ (layer_x, ln, lm_head_q8) and
# open_kernels/export_qwen36_kernels.py is the one command that produces these
# six xclbin/insts pairs plus a toolchain.json. Same rule as the BERT design
# sets: a binary beside the source that claims to produce it is a claim nobody
# checks, so the rebuild is the only way to get one. Shipped pre-built in the
# distributed package only.
# The trailing glob also covers the side-by-side variants an A/B leaves behind
# (open_kernels_q4_1, open_kernels_q8): same binaries, same rule.
src/xclbins/*/open_kernels*/

# repro-open-timeout.sh output (server logs, per-attempt client logs)
.repro-open-timeout/
.agents/logs/

# Local working notes, experiment logs and handoff documents. They are
# deliberately NOT committed: they are this investigation's scratch space, and
# several of them are megabytes of raw run output. The DURABLE record of a
# finding is its commit message and the test that pins it.
.local/
